    "## 3. Does it behave like a wave?\n",
    "\n",
    "Three checks before trusting any picture.\n",
    "\n",
    "**No trigonometry at runtime.** The honest test is not a grep, it is to disable `numpy`'s trigonometric functions and run the simulation anyway. If the update secretly relied on one, it would raise.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The front moves at the speed we asked for.** For a circular disturbance the edge should advance by $C$ cells per step.\n",
    "\n",
    "**It stays finite.** No NaNs, no overflow, energy bounded."
   ]
  },
