    "## 5. Overlapping waves\n",
    "\n",
    "Two drops, released at the same instant, a fixed distance apart. Where a crest from one meets a crest from the other the surface rises higher than either could alone. Where a crest meets a trough they cancel.\n",
    "\n",
    "The picture on the right is a slice through the middle row of cells. The lobes between the sources are the interference pattern: alternating bands of double height and near-zero height. No special code produces this. It falls out of adding four neighbours."
   ]
