    "## 6. Damping\n",
    "\n",
    "Three identical drops, three different loss coefficients, all photographed at the same step. Then the total energy of each run on a logarithmic axis.\n",
    "\n",
    "The straight line on a log axis is the signature of exponential decay, $E(t) \\approx E_0 e^{-\\alpha t}$, which is what a linear damping term is supposed to produce. A curved line would mean the model was losing energy in some other, unintended way."
   ]
