    "## 11. Limits, stated honestly\n",
    "\n",
    "- It is a linear model. Steep waves, breaking crests and wind-driven drift are nonlinear and out of scope.\n",
    "- The surface is one height field, not a full 3D fluid. No vertical velocity, no overturning.\n",
    "- The absorbing rim is good, not perfect. A small reflection remains, which is visible if you look closely at the edge.\n",
    "- The finite-difference stencil is second order in space and time. Smaller cells and smaller steps converge to the same behaviour, more slowly.\n",
    "- The speed is set by `C` and the cell size, so there is no separate dispersion relation here. Real water waves disperse, shallow-water waves less so."
   ]
  }
